OL,3,GNEWSAFamilies plea for help in 'cruel'
OL,4,Adementia battle
OL,5,
OL,6,FFamilies of loved ones with dementia
OL,7,Fhave described the challenges they face
OL,8,Fnavigating a system they say offers "no
OL,9,Fsupport" after diagnosis. Andy Burnham
OL,10,Fon Tuesday announced plans to create a
OL,11,Fnew national care service after his
OL,12,Flate father's experience.
OL,14,F"You see the person slipping away from
OL,15,Fyou, but you know they're going to slip
OL,16,Faway to a stage that's even worse,"
OL,17,Fsaid Jo Earlam, from Devon, who cared
OL,18,Ffor her husband John for almost a
OL,19,Fdecade.
OL,21,F"Dementia is a sad and cruel disease."
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
